<title>USA: GE unit files for $500 mln shelf preferred.</title>
<headline>GE unit files for $500 mln shelf preferred.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Capital Corp filed Tuesday with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $500 million in variable cumulative preferred stock.</p>
<p>The offering will consist of 5,000 preferred shares at a purchase price of $100,000 each, issuable in one or more series the General Electric unit said.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used to finance GECC's operations, the company said.</p>
